WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.860
Wait, we're talking about Frozen again?

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.700
Ugh, can't we just "let it go"?

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:21.560
*Holiday Intro Starts (Holiday Music Theme)*

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.780
Hello, Internet! Welcome to Film Theory!

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.660
The icy cold heart bringing a chill to the Disney canon.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.020
Case and point today, Frozen.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.540
You know those movies you love to watch over the holidays?

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:35.300
For Steph and I, it's always "The Nightmare Before Christmas" around Thanksgiving.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.420
And then "Lord of the Rings" and Disney leading up to Christmas.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:41.900
And with my tryptophan induced napping and Black Friday shopping behind me,

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.700
It meant that it was time for my yearly viewing of "Frozen."

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:48.720
And you know what? It's still a really good movie.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:52.060
I know it's easy to hate on it because of all the over-exposure it got,

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:56.160
but in all honestly the characters are great, the songs are great, it's really funny.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:01.380
So, Dear Internet, stop hating on popular things just to be all edgy and anti-culture. Ok?

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:08.960
You know, I say that, but then you gotta consider that a huge part of this movie's success was Disney's own willingness to hate on it's own established tropes.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.600
No one is saved by true love's kiss,

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:13.260
Everyone dismisses the idea of love at first sight,

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:16.340
And the dreamy "Prince Charming" turns out to be the villain.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:21.780
But ever since I watched the movie the first time, it's always been that last point that bothered me the most.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:26.080
Because for as much as I loved Prince Hans' turn to the dark side in the final moments of the movie,

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.600
It just felt like it... came out of nowhere.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:31.560
And of course, part of that is the point of the twist,

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:32.540
it's a surprise,

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:36.820
like that ream of printer paper your Aunt got you as a Christmas present that one time...

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:41.000
Man, you think reacting with enthusiasm to an ugly Christmas sweater is hard, try that one.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:45.940
But, if you actually stopped to watch Hans' behavior and the flow of his plan throughout the movie...

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:47.240
Nothing adds up...

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:47.920
Which means either,

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:53.640
A. Disney writers knew they wanted a big twist and used Hans to shuffle pieces around without much concern over how it played into his larger character arc.

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:57.480
Or B. There's something much more sinister going on in this world...

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:00.600
And while A. is probably the factually correct choice,

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.220
B. is the more fun choice,

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:03.180
and to me that means...

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:04.780
it's the right choice.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:09.740
So let's dedicate an episode to unearthing the secret conspiracy that clears Hans' name...

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:11.040
Once and for all.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:13.720
So let's first look at his motive for this big murder plot

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:14.860
He says himself,

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:22.460
"As 13th in line in my own Kingdom, I didn't stand a chance, I knew I'd have to marry into the throne somewhere"

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:24.720
Which on the surface would seem to make sense.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.660
He wants to rule the kingdom and he sees an opportunity with Arendal.

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.560
Marry one of the two princesses and boom!

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.520
He's in the running to be wearing the crown.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:34.020
And he gives us a little bit more detail in his next line:

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:38.800
"As heir, Elsa was preferable, of course, but no one was getting anywhere with her.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:44.120
But you, you were so desperate for love, you were willing to marry me just like that."

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:47.960
So option one is marry Elsa and fast-track your way up to the royal throne,

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:50.080
but since she tends to give people a bit of the old

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.360
"COLD SHOULDER"...

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:52.540
*comic rimshot*

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:55.400
I don't hear your raucous laughter, so let me shout it louder...

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:56.600
COLD

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:57.680
SHOULDER

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:58.340
BA DUM TS

00:02:58.340 --> 00:02:59.880
He went for the next best thing:

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:02.620
Anna, next in line to be queen, should Elsa die.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:03.500
And he knows this.

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:07.080
"I figured after we married, I'd have to stage a little accident for Elsa..."

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.740
Which anyone who's ever heard an evil monologue before those means

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:11.700
Giving her the old stab and a half,

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:13.700
Throwing her in front of a rogue snowplow

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:16.140
Or the classic bloodless Disney death of just

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:18.340
throwing her off a tall cliff, she's gone,

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:21.000
and Anna with Hans in tow ascent to the throne.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:25.540
"All that's left now is to kill Elsa and bring back summer."

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:28.980
This is the moment where things start to go off the rails.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:30.880
So his plan involves killing Elsa.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:32.520
He is so enthusiastic about it,

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:36.300
He mentions it TWICE in that little monologue we just went over.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:40.180
And yet, when he and the guards come to Elsa's ice palace, looking for Anna,

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:45.640
Hans expresses his intention to do the exact opposite: Protect Elsa.

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:49.320
"We're here to find Princess Anna, be on guard...

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.380
...but no harm is to come to the Queen."

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:54.840
Later in a scene where a guard literally has Elsa is his crosshairs,

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:57.760
Hans runs over and diverts the shot.

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:00.040
If he truly wants Elsa dead,

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:02.200
Why not let the guard kill her right then and there?

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:05.060
I mean, maybe he just really liked that snowplow idea,

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:07.120
But seriously, when life hands you lemons,

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:11.240
You shoot a crossbow bolt through the heart of the woman standing between you and the throne!

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:14.200
Hans' hands would be clean, and to the rest of the world,

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:18.230
Including Anna, who just got herself ice blasted by dear ol' sis,

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:20.880
Elsa is a threat. A MONSTER.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:22.760
But not only does he divert the shot,

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:26.280
He also offers her a nice bit of #MondayMotivation.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:28.740
"Don't be the monster they fear you are!"

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:32.960
HANS! Is this what you say to the person you have a murder plot against?

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.980
He's helping her to become a better person.

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:38.810
Seriously! She is on the verge of murdering people!

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:40.190
And that's no exaggeration.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:43.840
Look at this guard being shoved off the balcony by her ice wall.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:45.060
Had it not been for Hans,

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:47.200
She would have literally killed this man!

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:51.080
Disney's most beloved princess be killing some peeps up in this icy hizzouse!

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:52.740
The script even confirms it.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:55.640
Hans' line causes her to "snap out of her rage".

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:59.700
So WHY? Why would you help the woman you plan to eventually bump off,

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:03.860
When the problem solves itself right then and there in that moment?

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:04.780
And then again when they

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:06.680
bring Elsa back to Arendelle and put her

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:09.440
in prison he says once more- (Elsa): "why did you

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:11.660
bring me here?" (Hans): "I couldn't just let them

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:12.230
kill you"

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:14.270
"He's doing it to win on his trust" I hear

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:15.950
you say, but that's not it either! She's

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:17.600
already convinced she's in love with him.

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:19.430
In just a few scenes, she'll be begging

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:21.170
for Hans to kiss her. Anna: "Hans you have to

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:22.730
kiss me. Now!" And all through the

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:24.470
troll song both Christoph and Anna

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:26.420
continually assert that she's already a

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:28.280
taken woman; rejecting the idea that

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:30.290
there's any sort of romance there.

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:32.330
And here's the other thing, Hans is already

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:34.280
in charge of arendelle throughout most

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:36.290
of the movie. When Anna decides to run off

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:38.000
and bring back Elsa she puts him in charge.

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:41.500
Hans: "I'm coming with you."  Anna: "No I need you here,

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:43.810
to take care of Arendelle. I leave Prince Hans

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:44.650
in charge."

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:46.300
And let's face it Anna is just a few days

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:48.400
away from rising to the throne. Based on

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.440
the sisters talk, the ice castle, Elsa

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:52.690
has zero intention of returning to the

00:05:52.690 --> 00:06:00.550
city. Elsa : "Anna, please go back home, your life awaits. Go enjoy the sun and open up the

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:01.190
gates."

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:07.460
"Yes I'm alone, but I'm alone and free!" She's willingly abdicated the

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:08.060
throne.

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:09.560
She's saying that Anna now has the

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:11.000
power to keep the gates open because

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.460
she's the new decision-maker. Anna is

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:15.860
going to be the Queen. Elsa's happier

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:17.210
alone at the top of the mountain in her

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.190
fortress of solitude. Even when she

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.350
escapes prison, where's she running to? Her

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:24.800
safe space, the ice castle. So all Hans has

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:26.390
to do to accomplish his goal is to not

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:28.490
suck for the few days that Anna is away,

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:30.440
comfort her a bit when she returns home depressed

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:32.540
that Elsa is now ruling a private

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:34.610
snowman kingdom, and, you know make sure

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:37.310
that his future wife doesn't die. That's

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:39.380
all he has to do in order to achieve the

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:40.940
goal that he has set out to achieve;

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:43.550
literally do nothing. All the murder plots,

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:45.380
all the bringing Elsa back from the ice

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:46.160
castle,

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:48.590
none of it matters! But that last task is

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:50.090
important because let's actually talk

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:52.640
about his refusal to kiss Anna. So to recap:

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.710
Anna's heart has been frozen over by

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:56.690
Elsa's ice powers. She's about to die and

00:06:56.690 --> 00:06:58.550
needs an act of true love in order to

00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:00.260
save her. She thinks that this will be a

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:01.970
kiss from Hans because she's a Disney

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:03.530
character who was raised on Disney

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:06.260
movies apparently. But he refuses, making

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:08.690
it clear that he never loved her at all.

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:10.310
All he wanted to do was marry her for a

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:12.169
kingdom. He puts out the candle so she'll

00:07:12.169 --> 00:07:13.820
freeze to death faster and then leaves

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:15.770
prematurely because every villain always

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:18.560
leaves prematurely, except it makes zero

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:21.560
sense. There is literally no reason not

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:23.900
to kiss her in this situation. If she

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:24.470
lives, great!

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:26.330
He's able to be married to her and

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:28.760
rise to power at her side like his plan

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:31.430
always intended in the first place. If

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:33.800
the kiss doesn't work, well she dies and

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:35.150
he can still play the whole marriage

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:37.130
charade off. Just like he does in the

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:39.110
actual movie, except with someone who is

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:41.000
literally dead and can't show up a few

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:42.740
seconds later to disprove everything

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:44.690
that he just said. In fact if he truly

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.610
cares about his goal, well then he chose the

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:48.650
riskiest move he could have because

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.870
letting Anna die puts it in serious

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.880
jeopardy. If she doesn't make it, his

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:54.129
whole plan literally

00:07:54.129 --> 00:07:55.689
falls apart. To really

00:07:55.689 --> 00:07:57.369
understand why, though, we have to quickly

00:07:57.369 --> 00:07:59.289
talk about monarchies. I've been

00:07:59.289 --> 00:08:01.330
binge-watching the crown on netflix and

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.830
doing a bunch of research on royal

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:04.779
succession. You know, since my chances of being

00:08:04.779 --> 00:08:06.399
elected president here in the United

00:08:06.399 --> 00:08:08.169
States getting pretty slim these days

00:08:08.169 --> 00:08:10.179
-and hey why rule a united states when

00:08:10.179 --> 00:08:12.519
you can rule a united kingdom? Anyway if

00:08:12.519 --> 00:08:14.619
Arendelle is like most monarchies, Hans

00:08:14.619 --> 00:08:17.050
would have to keep Anna alive in order to

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:19.029
help her rule the kingdom. You see in a

00:08:19.029 --> 00:08:20.589
typical monarchy, like having Great

00:08:20.589 --> 00:08:22.149
Britain, the crown gets passed around

00:08:22.149 --> 00:08:24.399
based on the royal blood running through

00:08:24.399 --> 00:08:25.330
your veins.

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:27.580
So if a king or queen dies, the new ruler is

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:29.949
the oldest child. That's why Elsa becomes

00:08:29.949 --> 00:08:32.620
Queen. Her parents died, (maybe), but more on

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:33.339
that later....

00:08:33.339 --> 00:08:36.000
So when she's of age, she ascends to the throne;

00:08:36.339 --> 00:08:38.439
she's now the oldest blood relative.

00:08:38.439 --> 00:08:40.360
If Elsa abandons the throne, or gets

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:42.399
herself thrown in front of that snowplow and has

00:08:42.399 --> 00:08:44.649
no little Olafs of her own, it goes to

00:08:44.649 --> 00:08:45.759
the next in line: Anna.

00:08:45.759 --> 00:08:47.709
And that is what Hans should be

00:08:47.709 --> 00:08:50.139
counting on. But if Anna dies like she's

00:08:50.139 --> 00:08:51.910
literally minutes away from doing when

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:54.130
Hans decides to go all rogue, he doesn't

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:55.959
just remain on the throne and get to

00:08:55.959 --> 00:08:58.389
rule because of blood.

00:08:58.389 --> 00:09:00.009
Let me explain. Although many people

00:09:00.009 --> 00:09:01.569
consider every King to have a queen and

00:09:01.569 --> 00:09:02.529
vice versa,

00:09:02.529 --> 00:09:04.720
that's not really the way it works. The

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:06.220
one who possesses the royal blood is

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:08.230
called the monarch; that's the one who's

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.750
in charge. Their sexy Sven in the sheets

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:13.149
then is known as their royal consort and

00:09:13.149 --> 00:09:15.939
are in no way in line for the throne. For

00:09:15.939 --> 00:09:17.560
example, just look at the British line of

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:19.750
succession. The Queen's husband, Phillip,

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:21.670
isn't even in the top 50 when it comes

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:23.170
to waiting in line for the throne.

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:25.509
Mrs. Irina Walker Kruger who lives in

00:09:25.509 --> 00:09:27.399
the U.S. is more likely to become the

00:09:27.399 --> 00:09:29.019
next British monarch and she is

00:09:29.019 --> 00:09:31.000
currently on probation for being

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.130
associated with illegal gambling and

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:35.920
cockfighting. That is no joke. That person

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:37.240
is more likely to become the queen of

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:39.459
England than Phillip, the current Queen's

00:09:39.459 --> 00:09:40.870
husband. And based on how we see the

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:42.970
monarchy handoffs happening in Frozen

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:44.920
Arendelle would operate the same way.

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:46.870
Hans wouldn't even get the title of king

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:48.639
in his plan. Just like a deck of cards,

00:09:48.639 --> 00:09:50.889
the royal consort can't have a title

00:09:50.889 --> 00:09:52.870
that beats the actual monarch. So if

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:55.209
Anna is the Queen Hans can't be the

00:09:55.209 --> 00:09:55.750
king.

00:09:55.750 --> 00:09:57.529
It's the higher title.

00:09:57.529 --> 00:09:59.389
So instead Hans would always have to remain

00:09:59.389 --> 00:10:02.089
Prince Hans: royal consort to Queen

00:10:02.089 --> 00:10:03.589
Anna .It's actually the same thing in

00:10:03.589 --> 00:10:05.269
Britain right now. Queen Elizabeth is the

00:10:05.269 --> 00:10:06.709
reigning monarch and her husband is

00:10:06.709 --> 00:10:08.209
Prince Philip, even though he's a prince

00:10:08.209 --> 00:10:10.759
who is currently 95 years old. So you see,

00:10:10.759 --> 00:10:13.160
the crowd would go to literally anyone

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:15.589
with a drop of blood related to these

00:10:15.589 --> 00:10:18.589
two and Hans has zero Arenedellian blood

00:10:18.589 --> 00:10:20.749
blood. Get this, when it comes down to it,

00:10:20.749 --> 00:10:23.120
Tarzan would be next in line. It sounds

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:24.499
like a joke, but interviews with the

00:10:24.499 --> 00:10:26.480
creators of Frozen have confirmed that

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:28.699
Anna and Elsa's parents do survive their

00:10:28.699 --> 00:10:31.279
shipwreck and give birth to Tarzan,

00:10:31.279 --> 00:10:33.019
before of course they die from that

00:10:33.019 --> 00:10:35.389
grizzly leopard attack. Man! First a

00:10:35.389 --> 00:10:37.550
shipwreck, then mauled by a leopard.

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:39.439
Ho ho ho! (Christmas and all :) )Guess that's what you get for stifling

00:10:39.439 --> 00:10:42.949
your child ice magic. Karma is BRUTAL!

00:10:42.949 --> 00:10:44.839
if not Tarzan, then based on the

00:10:44.839 --> 00:10:46.519
other theories about the movie, including

00:10:46.519 --> 00:10:48.920
my last film theory about it, Rapunzel

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:51.290
could also be up for ruler of Arendelle.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:53.689
Regardless, if Hans has any hope of

00:10:53.689 --> 00:10:56.240
preserving a royal title and ruling the

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:59.600
kingdom in any way, he needs Anna alive;

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:01.430
making his evil turn here in the final

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:03.889
minutes of the movie make ZERO sense.

00:11:03.889 --> 00:11:06.079
But lastly let's just dial it back and

00:11:06.079 --> 00:11:07.879
look at how this guy behaves. When Anna

00:11:07.879 --> 00:11:09.319
leaves him in charge of the kingdom, he

00:11:09.319 --> 00:11:11.420
spends his time giving cloaks out to

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:12.980
people who are cold

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:15.649
Hans: "The castle is open, there is soup and hot

00:11:15.649 --> 00:11:17.899
glog in the Great Hall." He threatens to

00:11:17.899 --> 00:11:21.290
throw the Duke of Weaseltown- Duke:"Weselton"- in jail on

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:23.259
the charge of treason against Anna and

00:11:23.269 --> 00:11:25.370
Elsa Hans:"I will not hesitate to protect

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:26.930
Arendelle from treason!" When the Duke

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:29.449
complains about dangerous Elsa is, Hans

00:11:29.449 --> 00:11:31.639
corrects him saying: "You slipped on ice."

00:11:31.639 --> 00:11:33.559
Even at the very beginning of the movie,

00:11:33.559 --> 00:11:35.540
look at them look at each other, that's

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:37.819
genuine affection. And when Hans gets

00:11:37.819 --> 00:11:39.350
knocked into the water a few seconds

00:11:39.350 --> 00:11:40.910
later and is hidden under the boat,

00:11:40.910 --> 00:11:43.699
smiles to himself. Not an evil grin or

00:11:43.699 --> 00:11:45.350
sinister sneer it's just one of those

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:48.500
lovestruck goofy grins. In short, if this

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:50.509
is the guy who wants to rule Arendell and

00:11:50.509 --> 00:11:51.730
kill Elsa,

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:53.290
he's just not doing a good job of it. What's

00:11:53.290 --> 00:11:55.209
even stranger is that if there is a

00:11:55.209 --> 00:11:57.430
Frozen II the writers intend on giving

00:11:57.430 --> 00:12:00.040
Hans a redemption arc. No joke!

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:02.079
Santonio: "They're like, no no no, we have an idea. We

00:12:02.079 --> 00:12:04.180
wanna bring you back, we wanna redeem you." No

00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:06.040
other Disney villain has ever gotten

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:08.079
that sort of treatment. So what gives

00:12:08.079 --> 00:12:08.800
here?

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:10.959
Well what if Hans was just a pawn in

00:12:10.959 --> 00:12:13.240
someone else's game, collateral damage

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:16.269
for another's agenda? What if there's another

00:12:16.269 --> 00:12:19.720
villain in Frozen? No not Sven, not even

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:23.050
the Duke of Weaseltown. It's Olaf. Nope!

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:24.880
No, it's not Olaf, that would be stupid. The true

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:27.880
villains and Frozen are... the Trolls? You heard

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:29.380
me, those cuddly little rocks that are

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:31.300
just randomly shoved into the movie may

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:33.820
just be the ones with the evil intent.

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:35.860
now that may seem like a stretch, but hear

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:36.579
me out here.

00:12:36.579 --> 00:12:38.079
Let's start with their song "Fixer-Upper",

00:12:38.079 --> 00:12:39.250
which at first seems like a

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:40.839
light-hearted comedy song, but when you

00:12:40.839 --> 00:12:42.490
actually bothered to pay attention to

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:44.230
the lyrics, they contain some really

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:45.970
disturbing lines. Like i mentioned

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:48.399
earlier, Christoph is VERY upfront about Anna

00:12:48.399 --> 00:12:51.310
already being engaged to Hans. Christoph: "She's

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:52.839
engaged to someone else,

00:12:52.839 --> 00:12:55.300
okay?!" And yet despite this, the trolls

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:57.670
steamroll past that little detail saying

00:12:57.670 --> 00:13:00.040
her "engagement is a flex

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:02.620
arrangement.." and "get the fiancé out of

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:04.029
the way and the whole thing will be

00:13:04.029 --> 00:13:06.160
fixed." By the end of the song, the Trolls

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:08.350
are literally trying to trick Anna into

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:12.160
marrying Christoph. Pastor Troll: "Do you, Anna, take Christoph to be

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:14.680
your trollfully wedded-" Anna: "-Wait what?" Pastor Troll: "You're

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:16.510
getting married.'' Willfully ignoring that

00:13:16.510 --> 00:13:17.920
she probably doesn't want to kiss a guy

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:19.839
who literally eats carrots that came out

00:13:19.839 --> 00:13:22.000
of his reindeers mouth. But why would

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.949
they pushed so hard to see these two

00:13:23.949 --> 00:13:26.230
married? Well remember, Christoph was adopted

00:13:26.230 --> 00:13:28.660
by the trolls; he's part of the clan. So having

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:30.130
one of their own be a part of the noble

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:33.040
family is a huge deal, especially when

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.019
the nobles think you look like this.

00:13:35.019 --> 00:13:36.699
That's some pretty sinister-looking imagery

00:13:36.699 --> 00:13:38.949
right there, just saying. also ask

00:13:38.949 --> 00:13:39.880
yourself this:

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:42.100
who were the first ones to scare Elsa

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:44.649
about her powers? The Trolls. Prior to

00:13:44.649 --> 00:13:46.660
visiting them, Elsa was confident in her

00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:47.380
abilities.

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:49.240
The only reason Anna gets injured at

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:50.920
the start of the movies is because she was

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:53.199
reckless, leaving Elsa as the one who has

00:13:53.199 --> 00:13:54.620
to take all the blame.

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:57.410
Dad: "Elsa, what have you done?!" And yet when Mom Frozen

00:13:57.410 --> 00:13:59.210
and Dad Frozen take their daughters to

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:01.220
see good old grandpappy, what's the

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:03.380
solution? He does the following:

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:06.350
"I recommend we remove all magic, even

00:14:06.350 --> 00:14:10.580
memories of magic, to be safe." Remove all magic,

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:11.570
he said. Huh

00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:14.090
Did Anna never have powers too? Strange.

00:14:14.090 --> 00:14:15.470
Anyway, let me put that one of the old

00:14:15.470 --> 00:14:17.210
list of potential theories to look

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:17.510
into.

00:14:17.510 --> 00:14:19.160
Regardless what does erasing Anna's

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:21.260
memories do? NOTHING. Well, at least nothing

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:22.190
GOOD.

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:23.810
She becomes alone and alienated from

00:14:23.810 --> 00:14:26.120
a sister for reason she can't fathom.

00:14:26.120 --> 00:14:28.070
Meanwhile, Elsa is pushed into a kingdom

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:30.020
of isolation, where it looks like she's

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:31.820
the queen. Pappy blue ribbon over here

00:14:31.820 --> 00:14:34.580
also ensures that Elsa is terrified of

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:37.250
herself. Grandpappy Troll: "You must learn to control it.

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:42.350
Fear will be your enemy." You sure about

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:43.910
that Grandpappy? You're gonna say that

00:14:43.910 --> 00:14:45.260
fear IS the ultimate enemy and then

00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:48.050
punctuate the moment by doing what now?

00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:51.320
SCARING her with a spooky vision. Alright

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:52.190
Cool.

00:14:52.190 --> 00:14:54.500
Good on you. To quote the script, "The

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:56.570
spikes turn into human form which

00:14:56.570 --> 00:14:59.060
then attack the silhouette of adult Elsa.

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:02.180
This frightens Elsa." Grandpappy (MatPat's amazing impersination): "Fear is going to be

00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:04.730
your enemy- BOO! Gotcha!" Good one grandpappy.

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:07.490
It's like the worst jump-scare ever. Should put you into FNAF

00:15:07.490 --> 00:15:09.950
Sister Location custom night. All of

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:12.260
this even though, once again, Elsa was

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:14.300
fine and had perfect control of her

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:16.460
powers before this visit.

00:15:16.460 --> 00:15:18.140
What else to the trolls do? Oh yeah! They

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:20.210
willfully mislead Anna into thinking that

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:22.400
she needs true love's kiss to survive

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:24.260
her frozen heart, despite them being love

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:26.060
experts and also completely wrong.

00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:29.030
Woman Troll: "A true love's kiss, perhaps?" But here's the

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:31.850
big problem: Grandpappy is really good at

00:15:31.850 --> 00:15:33.950
manipulating people's minds, and he does

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:35.630
it all the time.

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:37.430
Sure in Frozen, we only see it done once

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:39.860
to Anna, which as I said accomplishes

00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:42.410
nothing good. But then Once Upon a Time's

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:44.630
Frozen themed season, we see him do it again,

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:47.090
and this time on a much larger and much

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:49.250
more catastrophic scale. when Gerta(I thought it was Iduna?),

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:50.930
eventual queen of Arendelle and mother

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:53.270
of Anna and Elsa traps her sister in a magical

00:15:53.270 --> 00:15:55.340
urn, because that sister killed her

00:15:55.340 --> 00:15:58.340
other sister- WORST DAY EVER -she asks

00:15:58.340 --> 00:15:59.660
Grandpappy for help,

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:01.100
requesting that he erase the memories

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:04.010
of the ENTIRE kingdom of Arendelle to

00:16:04.010 --> 00:16:05.100
never remember

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:07.800
her two sisters. And Pappy, he just does it.

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:09.750
He puts up no resistance, requests no

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:11.370
payment, he's just like, "All right let's

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:12.600
create some fake memories in these

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:15.000
peasants" And THEN he even lies to cover

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:16.980
it up! When Anna asks him about the

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:18.630
incident, he hides the fact that it was

00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:20.670
Ana's mother who requested the memory

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:22.140
wipe in the first place.

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:25.260
He's protecting a legacy of lies. So what's to say

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:27.480
that the trolls couldn't - or wouldn't - do

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:29.490
some sort of memory magic on Hans,

00:16:29.490 --> 00:16:31.410
the fiancé who just happens to be in the

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:33.750
way of their big plans for Christoph.

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:36.450
Remember what the trolls say over and over again, Grandpappy: "The head

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:38.070
can be persuaded,

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:41.670
but the heart is not so easily changed."

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:44.490
Long story short, Hans's plan makes zero

00:16:44.490 --> 00:16:46.200
sense, especially considering all the

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:48.090
steps he makes counter to it earlier in

00:16:48.090 --> 00:16:48.780
the movie.

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:51.180
All he needed was that final kiss, and he

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:53.040
was locked in, making his turn to be the

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:54.600
villain in that final moment of the

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:57.000
movie the complete antithesis of what he

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:59.220
was looking to accomplish. But it does

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:01.140
make sense if you consider the Trolls

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:03.150
wanted to throw that fiancé away and

00:17:03.150 --> 00:17:05.550
get Christoph inserted in his place.

00:17:05.550 --> 00:17:06.750
They've shown themselves to have the

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:08.400
means to manipulate unsuspecting

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:10.440
innocent minds, the cunning to conceal

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:12.810
their deeds, and the motivations to trick

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:14.700
people into getting what they want.

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:16.050
Maybe the redemption arc the writers

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:17.970
have planned for Hans in Frozen 2 is

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:19.920
less about a bad guy turning good, but

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:22.050
rather a good guy getting to reveal the

00:17:22.050 --> 00:17:25.050
true villains acting behind the scenes.

00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:29.640
But hey! that's just a theory. A FILM

00:17:29.640 --> 00:17:32.900
THEORY! AAAAAAAAND CUT!

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:50.000
(OUTRO)

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:54.000
Thanks for reading my subtitles! ;)

